    "notes": "Reviewed every take by contact strip. The walk keeps its published version. The attack took five takes: the first two cut the whirling chain at the top or left edge, and the reel-in retakes strobed dark or still swung the hook wide, so the attack is the fifth take with the five frames where the hook crosses the canvas edge skipped. The hit is retaken with room below for the stagger, and the cast is retaken with room above and steady light. The defend ends on the held guard before its dark plates. Idle, defend and death are first takes."
